      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems VERY typo-prone.  That is, all I need to do is drop the \u0027-\u0027 when passing an error return code and it\u0027ll be interpreted as a valid size.\n\nIt\u0027s safer to pass a second param where the handler stores the response size:\n\n    int *response_size_ptr;\n\nThe host command handler should initialize that to 0 before calling the handler, so that only handlers which return data need touch it.\n\nHaven\u0027t decided whether we should restructure the LPC protocol to pass the parameters size somehow, so that handlers can ensure they got all their data.  While we\u0027re doing that, do we want a checksum/CRC for the parameter data so we can ensure integrity?",
      "revId": "6a28edf02996ddf6b7f32a3831d07d5f0271848f",
